window.REV_FLIP=window.REV_FLIP||{};window.REV_FLIP["github-actions"]=[{"id":"github-actions-f0001","card":"q-github-actions-001-ci-cd-concepts","sec":"github-actions-s002","q":"What is CI/CD, and how does it benefit software teams?","a":"<p>CI/CD automates code integration, testing and deployment. Benefits: faster feedback, fewer bugs, better collaboration, quicker releases.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0002","card":"q-github-actions-001-ci-cd-concepts","sec":"github-actions-s002","q":"What is the difference between Continuous Integration, Continuous Delivery and Continuous Deployment?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Continuous Integration: frequent code merges with automated tests.</li>\n  <li>Continuous Delivery: CI plus an automated release, with a manual deploy step.</li>\n  <li>Continuous Deployment: CI plus automated deployment to production.</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0003","card":"q-github-actions-001-ci-cd-concepts","sec":"github-actions-s002","q":"What are the key components of a CI/CD pipeline?","a":"<p>Source control, build, test, deploy, monitoring.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0004","card":"q-github-actions-001-ci-cd-concepts","sec":"github-actions-s002","q":"How does GitHub Actions fit into the CI/CD ecosystem?","a":"<p>It automates CI/CD workflows inside GitHub using YAML, integrating with repos and tools such as Docker and AWS.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0005","card":"q-github-actions-001-ci-cd-concepts","sec":"github-actions-s002","q":"What are some common use cases for GitHub Actions beyond CI/CD?","a":"<p>Automation (issue labeling), code review (linting), notifications and scheduled tasks.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0006","card":"q-github-actions-002-github-actions-compared-with-jenkins-and","sec":"github-actions-s003","q":"What are GitHub Actions, and how do they differ from traditional CI/CD tools like Jenkins or CircleCI?","a":"<p>GitHub Actions is a built-in GitHub tool for automating workflows (build, test, deploy) using YAML files triggered by repo events. Jenkins is standalone, plugin-heavy and flexible. CircleCI is cloud-focused and orb-based. GitHub Actions is tightly integrated with GitHub, simpler to set up, and uses a marketplace of reusable actions.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0007","card":"q-github-actions-002-github-actions-compared-with-jenkins-and","sec":"github-actions-s003","q":"What are the main advantages of GitHub Actions over Jenkins or CircleCI?","a":"<p>GitHub integration, easy YAML setup, the action marketplace, a free tier and scalable runners.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0008","card":"q-github-actions-002-github-actions-compared-with-jenkins-and","sec":"github-actions-s003","q":"What file format is used for workflows, and why?","a":"<p>YAML. It is readable, simple and widely used in CI/CD for structured automation.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0009","card":"q-github-actions-003-workflows-and-the-workflows-directory","sec":"github-actions-s004","q":"What is a workflow in GitHub Actions, and how is it defined?","a":"<p>A workflow is an automated process made of jobs, triggered by events. It is defined in a YAML file under <code>.github/workflows/</code>, specifying a name, triggers (<code>on</code>) and jobs.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0010","card":"q-github-actions-003-workflows-and-the-workflows-directory","sec":"github-actions-s004","q":"What is the purpose of the <code>.github/workflows</code> directory?","a":"<p>It holds all workflow YAML files. GitHub looks there to find and run automation when events occur.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0011","card":"q-github-actions-003-workflows-and-the-workflows-directory","sec":"github-actions-s004","q":"What are the key components of a workflow file?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>name</strong>: workflow label.</li>\n  <li><strong>on</strong>: event triggers (for example <code>push</code>).</li>\n  <li><strong>jobs</strong>: tasks to run, each with <code>runs-on</code> (runner type) and steps (actions or commands).</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0012","card":"q-github-actions-003-workflows-and-the-workflows-directory","sec":"github-actions-s004","q":"What is the typical structure of a <code>.yml</code> workflow file?","a":"<p><code>name</code>, <code>on</code> (triggers), then <code>jobs</code> containing <code>runs-on</code> and <code>steps</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0013","card":"q-github-actions-003-workflows-and-the-workflows-directory","sec":"github-actions-s004","q":"What is the purpose of the <code>on</code> keyword?","a":"<p>It defines the events (such as push or pull_request) that trigger the workflow.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0014","card":"q-github-actions-004-events-jobs-and-steps","sec":"github-actions-s005","q":"What is an event, and what are common examples?","a":"<p>An event triggers a workflow. Common ones: <code>push</code> (code push), <code>pull_request</code> (PR activity), <code>schedule</code> (cron-based) and <code>workflow_dispatch</code> (manual).</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0015","card":"q-github-actions-004-events-jobs-and-steps","sec":"github-actions-s005","q":"What is the difference between a job and a step?","a":"<p>A job is a group of steps that run on one runner. A step is an individual task (checkout, run a script) inside a job. Jobs can run in parallel by default; steps run sequentially.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0016","card":"q-github-actions-005-actions-and-the-checkout-action","sec":"github-actions-s006","q":"What are actions, and how do you use pre-built ones?","a":"<p>Actions are reusable units of work. Pre-built ones from the Marketplace (for example <code>actions/checkout@v4</code>) are used with <code>uses</code> inside steps.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>steps:\n  - uses: actions/checkout@v4</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0017","card":"q-github-actions-005-actions-and-the-checkout-action","sec":"github-actions-s006","q":"What is <code>actions/checkout</code>, and why is it used so often?","a":"<p>It clones the repo's code onto the runner, which build and test steps need.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0018","card":"q-github-actions-006-runners","sec":"github-actions-s007","q":"What is the role of runners, and what types exist?","a":"<p>Runners are VMs or containers that execute workflows. GitHub-hosted runners are <code>ubuntu-latest</code>, <code>windows-latest</code> and <code>macos-latest</code>. Self-hosted runners are your own machines.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0019","card":"q-github-actions-006-runners","sec":"github-actions-s007","q":"What does <code>runs-on</code> do, and what are the common values?","a":"<p>It sets the runner type: <code>ubuntu-latest</code>, <code>windows-latest</code>, <code>macos-latest</code> or <code>self-hosted</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0020","card":"q-github-actions-007-specifying-events","sec":"github-actions-s008","q":"How do you specify the events that trigger a workflow?","a":"<p>Use <code>on</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on:\n  push:\n  pull_request:\n  schedule:\n    - cron: &#x27;0 0 * * *&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0021","card":"q-github-actions-008-branch-tag-and-path-filters","sec":"github-actions-s009","q":"How do you run a workflow only on specific branches or tags?","a":"<p>Use <code>branches</code> or <code>tags</code> filters under the event.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n    tags: [&#x27;v*&#x27;]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0022","card":"q-github-actions-008-branch-tag-and-path-filters","sec":"github-actions-s009","q":"How do you run a workflow only when certain files change (for example <code>.py</code> files)?","a":"<p>Use a <code>paths</code> filter.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on:\n  push:\n    paths:\n      - &#x27;**/*.py&#x27;\njobs:\n  check:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - run: python -m py_compile *.py</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0023","card":"q-github-actions-008-branch-tag-and-path-filters","sec":"github-actions-s009","q":"How do you run jobs by change type in a monorepo (frontend vs backend)?","a":"<p>Use <code>paths</code> (or <code>if</code> with change detection).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on:\n  push:\n    paths: [&#x27;services/frontend/**&#x27;]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0024","card":"q-github-actions-008-branch-tag-and-path-filters","sec":"github-actions-s009","q":"How do you run a job only when <code>README.md</code> changes?","a":"<p>Check the commit's modified files with an <code>if</code> on the job.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>jobs:\n  check:\n    if: contains(github.event.commits[0].modified, &#x27;README.md&#x27;)\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n      - run: echo &quot;README.md modified!&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0025","card":"q-github-actions-009-manual-and-scheduled-triggers","sec":"github-actions-s010","q":"How can you trigger a workflow manually or on a schedule?","a":"<p>Manual: <code>workflow_dispatch</code>, optionally with inputs. Schedule: <code>schedule</code> with a cron expression.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on:\n  workflow_dispatch:\n    inputs:\n      environment:\n        description: &#x27;Environment&#x27;\n        required: true\n        default: &#x27;staging&#x27;\njobs:\n  deploy:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - run: echo &quot;Deploying to ${{ github.event.inputs.environment }}&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0026","card":"q-github-actions-009-manual-and-scheduled-triggers","sec":"github-actions-s010","q":"How do you schedule a workflow (daily, weekly, every 15 minutes)?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on:\n  schedule:\n    - cron: &#x27;0 0 * * *&#x27;     # daily at midnight\n    # - cron: &#x27;0 9 * * 1&#x27;   # every Monday at 9 AM\n    # - cron: &#x27;*/15 * * * *&#x27; # every 15 minutes\njobs:\n  task:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - run: ./my-script.sh</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0027","card":"q-github-actions-010-cross-repository-triggers","sec":"github-actions-s011","q":"How can you trigger a workflow in one repository from another?","a":"<p>Use <code>repository_dispatch</code> in the target workflow and call the GitHub API from the other repo.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on:\n  repository_dispatch:\n    types: [trigger]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0028","card":"q-github-actions-011-environment-variables-and-contexts","sec":"github-actions-s012","q":"How do you define environment variables?","a":"<p>Use <code>env</code> at workflow, job or step level.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>env:\n  GLOBAL: &quot;value&quot;\njobs:\n  build:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    env:\n      JOB: &quot;job-value&quot;\n    steps:\n      - env:\n          STEP: &quot;step-value&quot;\n        run: echo $STEP</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0029","card":"q-github-actions-011-environment-variables-and-contexts","sec":"github-actions-s012","q":"What is the <code>env</code> context compared with <code>github</code> and <code>secrets</code>?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>env</strong>: custom variables (<code>${{ env.VAR }}</code>).</li>\n  <li><strong>github</strong>: event data (<code>${{ github.sha }}</code>).</li>\n  <li><strong>secrets</strong>: secure data (<code>${{ secrets.KEY }}</code>).</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0030","card":"q-github-actions-012-running-steps-in-a-container","sec":"github-actions-s013","q":"How can you use Docker containers in a workflow?","a":"<p>Run the job in a container with <code>container</code>, or call Docker commands in steps.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>container: node:16</code></pre></div>\n<p>A job-level container can also be written with <code>image</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>jobs:\n  custom:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    container:\n      image: node:16\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n      - run: node --version</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0031","card":"q-github-actions-013-matrix-builds","sec":"github-actions-s014","q":"How do you set up a matrix strategy?","a":"<p>Use <code>strategy.matrix</code> to run a job across configurations such as OS or language versions.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>jobs:\n  test:\n    runs-on: ${{ matrix.os }}\n    strategy:\n      matrix:\n        os: [ubuntu-latest, windows-latest]\n        node: [14, 16]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0032","card":"q-github-actions-013-matrix-builds","sec":"github-actions-s014","q":"How do you test across multiple versions of a language?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>strategy:\n  matrix:\n    python-version: [&#x27;3.8&#x27;, &#x27;3.9&#x27;]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0033","card":"q-github-actions-013-matrix-builds","sec":"github-actions-s014","q":"How do you run integration tests across Node.js versions?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on: push\njobs:\n  test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    strategy:\n      matrix:\n        node-version: [14, 16, 18]\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n        with:\n          node-version: ${{ matrix.node-version }}\n      - run: npm install &amp;&amp; npm run integration-tests</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0034","card":"q-github-actions-013-matrix-builds","sec":"github-actions-s014","q":"How do you test on Windows and Linux?","a":"<p>Use an OS matrix, and set <code>shell: bash</code> so the same script works on both.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>strategy:\n  matrix:\n    os: [ubuntu-latest, windows-latest]\nsteps:\n  - run: echo &quot;Cross-platform&quot;\n    shell: bash</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0035","card":"q-github-actions-013-matrix-builds","sec":"github-actions-s014","q":"Matrix test across Ubuntu, macOS and Windows?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>jobs:\n  test:\n    runs-on: ${{ matrix.os }}\n    strategy: { matrix: { os: [ubuntu-latest, macos-latest, windows-latest] } }\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n      - run: echo &quot;Testing on ${{ matrix.os }}&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0036","card":"q-github-actions-014-job-dependencies-with-needs","sec":"github-actions-s015","q":"What is the purpose of <code>needs</code>?","a":"<p>It makes a job run only after the listed jobs finish successfully.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>jobs:\n  build:\n  deploy:\n    needs: build</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0037","card":"q-github-actions-014-job-dependencies-with-needs","sec":"github-actions-s015","q":"How do you run a security scan after the build?","a":"<p>Put the scan in its own job with <code>needs: build</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>jobs:\n  build:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n      - run: echo &quot;Building...&quot;\n  scan:\n    needs: build\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n      - run: echo &quot;Scanning...&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0038","card":"q-github-actions-015-passing-data-between-steps","sec":"github-actions-s016","q":"How do you pass outputs between steps?","a":"<p>Write <code>name=value</code> to <code>$GITHUB_OUTPUT</code> in a step with an <code>id</code>, then read <code>steps.&lt;id&gt;.outputs.&lt;name&gt;</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>steps:\n  - id: step1\n    run: echo &quot;output=hello&quot; &gt;&gt; $GITHUB_OUTPUT\n  - run: echo ${{ steps.step1.outputs.output }}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0039","card":"q-github-actions-015-passing-data-between-steps","sec":"github-actions-s016","q":"How can you share data between steps in a job?","a":"<p>Use files, <code>GITHUB_ENV</code>, or artifacts.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- run: echo &quot;VAR=value&quot; &gt;&gt; $GITHUB_ENV\n- run: echo ${{ env.VAR }}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0040","card":"q-github-actions-016-conditional-execution","sec":"github-actions-s017","q":"What is the <code>if</code> conditional, and how is it used?","a":"<p>It controls whether a step or job runs, using expressions.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>steps:\n  - if: github.event_name == &#x27;push&#x27;\n    run: echo &quot;Push only&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0041","card":"q-github-actions-016-conditional-execution","sec":"github-actions-s017","q":"How do you run steps differently for pull requests and pushes?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>steps:\n  - if: github.event_name == &#x27;pull_request&#x27;\n    run: npm test\n  - if: github.event_name == &#x27;push&#x27;\n    run: npm run deploy</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0042","card":"q-github-actions-016-conditional-execution","sec":"github-actions-s017","q":"How do you run a job only on a given branch?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>jobs:\n  build:\n    if: github.ref == &#x27;refs/heads/main&#x27;\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n      - run: echo &quot;Building on main&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0043","card":"q-github-actions-016-conditional-execution","sec":"github-actions-s017","q":"How do you handle failures (for example continue on error)?","a":"<p>Use <code>continue-on-error: true</code> on a step, or <code>if: failure()</code> to run a step after a failure. Combine them to handle errors gracefully, and avoid overusing <code>continue-on-error</code> because it can mask real issues.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>steps:\n  - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n  - name: Optional step\n    continue-on-error: true\n    run: curl http://optional-service.com\n  - name: Log if failed\n    if: failure()\n    run: echo &quot;Optional step failed, continuing&quot;\n  - name: Critical step\n    run: ./build.sh</code></pre></div>\n<p>Typical uses of <code>continue-on-error</code>: notifications to services that may be down, optional linting, and metrics collection that is not critical to deployment.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0044","card":"q-github-actions-017-timeouts","sec":"github-actions-s018","q":"What is <code>timeout-minutes</code>, and why use it?","a":"<p>It cancels a job or step after a time limit, which prevents hangs.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>jobs:\n  build:\n    timeout-minutes: 10</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0045","card":"q-github-actions-018-concurrency-control","sec":"github-actions-s019","q":"How does GitHub Actions handle concurrency control?","a":"<p><code>concurrency</code> limits simultaneous runs in a group and can cancel in-progress runs for the same context.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\nconcurrency:\n  group: ${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}\n  cancel-in-progress: true</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0046","card":"q-github-actions-019-secrets","sec":"github-actions-s020","q":"How does GitHub Actions handle secrets, and why does it matter?","a":"<p>Secrets are encrypted variables set in repository settings and read as <code>${{ secrets.NAME }}</code>. They are masked in logs. They keep sensitive data such as API keys out of the code.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0047","card":"q-github-actions-019-secrets","sec":"github-actions-s020","q":"How do you use a secret in a step?","a":"<p>Pass it through <code>env</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>steps:\n  - env:\n      API_KEY: ${{ secrets.API_KEY }}\n    run: ./deploy.sh</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0048","card":"q-github-actions-019-secrets","sec":"github-actions-s020","q":"How do you secure a workflow that calls an external API needing auth?","a":"<p>Store the key in secrets, reference <code>${{ secrets.KEY }}</code>, and keep it out of logs.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>env:\n  API_KEY: ${{ secrets.API_KEY }}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0049","card":"q-github-actions-020-github-token-versus-a-personal-access-to","sec":"github-actions-s021","q":"What is <code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code>, and how does it differ from a PAT?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>GITHUB_TOKEN</strong>: created automatically for each run, scoped to the repo, expires when the run ends.</li>\n  <li><strong>PAT</strong>: created by a user, customizable scope, persistent.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- run: curl -H &quot;Authorization: token ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}&quot; https://api.github.com/repos/${{ github.repository }}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0050","card":"q-github-actions-022-securing-a-workflow","sec":"github-actions-s023","q":"How can you secure a workflow against unauthorized access or misuse?","a":"<p>Use secrets, limit <code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code> permissions, pin actions to a version or commit SHA, use environments, control concurrency and audit workflows. Avoid logging secrets.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>name: Secure Workflow\non: push\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n  issues: write\nconcurrency:\n  group: ${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}\n  cancel-in-progress: true\njobs:\n  deploy:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3.0.0\n      - name: Deploy with secret\n        env:\n          API_KEY: ${{ secrets.API_KEY }}\n        run: ./deploy.sh</code></pre></div>\n<p>The token is limited to reading contents and writing issues, <code>checkout</code> is pinned, the secret is passed through <code>env</code>, and only one run per branch executes at a time.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0051","card":"q-github-actions-023-environments","sec":"github-actions-s024","q":"What are GitHub Actions environments, and how are they used in deployments?","a":"<p>Environments represent deployment targets (dev, staging, production) with protection rules (such as approvals), secrets and variables.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0052","card":"q-github-actions-023-environments","sec":"github-actions-s024","q":"How do you deploy to dev, staging and prod with different configs?","a":"<p>Use environments, environment-specific secrets, conditional jobs and approvals.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>jobs:\n  deploy-prod:\n    environment: production\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - run: ./deploy.sh</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0053","card":"q-github-actions-024-credentials-exposed-in-a-repo","sec":"github-actions-s025","q":"A junior developer pushes credentials to a public repo. How do you mitigate and prevent it?","a":"<p>Remove the credentials, rotate the secrets, move them into GitHub Secrets, enable secret scanning and train the team. Remove the secret from history as well.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- run: deploy.sh\n  env:\n    API_KEY: ${{ secrets.API_KEY }}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0054","card":"q-github-actions-025-security-scans-before-deployment","sec":"github-actions-s026","q":"How do you run a security scan before deployment?","a":"<p>Use Dependabot or tools such as Snyk, and fail the job on vulnerabilities.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- run: snyk test\n  env:\n    SNYK_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.SNYK_TOKEN }}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0055","card":"q-github-actions-026-caching-dependencies","sec":"github-actions-s027","q":"How does GitHub Actions support caching, and what are the steps to cache npm or pip?","a":"<p><code>actions/cache</code> stores files or directories under a unique key and restores them when the key matches. If there is no match, a new cache is saved for future runs. The cache is scoped to the repository and branch, with optional restore from parent branches.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>path</strong>: files or directories to cache (<code>~/.m2/repository</code>, <code>node_modules</code>, <code>~/.npm</code>, <code>~/.cache/pip</code>).</li>\n  <li><strong>key</strong>: unique identifier, usually including a file hash so the cache is invalidated when dependencies change.</li>\n  <li><strong>restore-keys</strong>: fallback keys used when the primary key does not match.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Use cases: build tools (Maven, Gradle), package managers (npm, Yarn, pip), compiled artifacts and intermediate build outputs. Use <code>hashFiles</code> on dependency files (<code>pom.xml</code>, <code>package-lock.json</code>) and specify multiple paths for complex projects.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0056","card":"q-github-actions-028-speeding-up-a-slow-workflow","sec":"github-actions-s029","q":"A workflow takes too long and delays feedback. How do you optimize it?","a":"<p>Cache dependencies, parallelize jobs, skip unnecessary steps with <code>if</code>, optimize commands and use faster runners.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0057","card":"q-github-actions-028-speeding-up-a-slow-workflow","sec":"github-actions-s029","q":"A workflow is too slow (about 20 minutes). What do you do?","a":"<p>The same measures: cache, parallelize, skip steps.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0058","card":"q-github-actions-028-speeding-up-a-slow-workflow","sec":"github-actions-s029","q":"A workflow fails intermittently because of network issues while downloading dependencies. How do you fix it?","a":"<p>Cache dependencies, use a proxy, retry steps and increase timeouts.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- uses: nick-invision/retry@v2\n  with:\n    command: npm install</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0059","card":"q-github-actions-029-reducing-actions-minutes","sec":"github-actions-s030","q":"A workflow exceeds the free-tier minutes. How do you analyze and reduce usage?","a":"<p>Check billing, cache dependencies, limit triggers, and use self-hosted runners.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0060","card":"q-github-actions-029-reducing-actions-minutes","sec":"github-actions-s030","q":"A pipeline consumes too many minutes. How do you reduce them?","a":"<p>Cache dependencies, parallelize, skip steps and use self-hosted runners.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0061","card":"q-github-actions-030-artifacts","sec":"github-actions-s031","q":"What are artifacts, and how are they used?","a":"<p>Artifacts are files (builds, reports) uploaded with <code>actions/upload-artifact</code> for sharing between jobs or for debugging.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>name: Upload Artifact\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\njobs:\n  build:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n      - run: zip -r build.zip .\n      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v3\n        with:\n          name: build-artifact\n          path: build.zip</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0062","card":"q-github-actions-030-artifacts","sec":"github-actions-s031","q":"How do you run a linter and upload its output?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>steps:\n  - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n  - run: npm install &amp;&amp; npm run lint &gt; lint-output.txt 2&gt;&amp;1\n  - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v3\n    with:\n      name: lint-report\n      path: lint-output.txt</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0063","card":"q-github-actions-030-artifacts","sec":"github-actions-s031","q":"How do you clean old artifacts after a run?","a":"<p>Use a cleanup step that only runs on success.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- if: success()\n  uses: actions/delete-package-versions@v4\n  with:\n    package-type: &#x27;artifact&#x27;\n    min-versions-to-keep: 1</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0064","card":"q-github-actions-031-composite-actions","sec":"github-actions-s032","q":"What are composite actions, and how do you create one?","a":"<p>A composite action bundles steps into one reusable unit. Create it in <code>.github/actions/my-action/action.yml</code>. Each <code>run</code> step needs a <code>shell</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>name: &#x27;My Action&#x27;\nruns:\n  using: &#x27;composite&#x27;\n  steps:\n    - run: echo &quot;Step 1&quot;\n      shell: bash\n    - run: echo &quot;Step 2&quot;\n      shell: bash</code></pre></div>\n<p>Use it with <code>uses: ./.github/actions/my-action</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0065","card":"q-github-actions-032-reusable-workflows","sec":"github-actions-s033","q":"What are reusable workflows, and when would you use them?","a":"<p>They are callable YAML workflows for shared tasks, used to standardize pipelines. Define one with <code>workflow_call</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code># .github/workflows/reusable.yml\non:\n  workflow_call:\n    inputs:\n      param:\n        required: true\n        type: string\njobs:\n  run:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - run: echo ${{ inputs.param }}</code></pre></div>\n<p>Call it from another workflow:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>jobs:\n  call:\n    uses: ./.github/workflows/reusable.yml\n    with:\n      param: &quot;Hello&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0066","card":"q-github-actions-034-deprecated-actions-and-microservices","sec":"github-actions-s035","q":"An action you use is deprecated. What do you do?","a":"<p>Update to a newer version or replicate its behavior manually.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- uses: actions/setup-node@v4</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0067","card":"q-github-actions-034-deprecated-actions-and-microservices","sec":"github-actions-s035","q":"How do you set up CI/CD for microservices in separate repos?","a":"<p>Standardize with reusable workflows, keep repo-specific configs, manage secrets centrally and use cross-repo triggers.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>jobs:\n  build:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n      - run: npm test</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0068","card":"q-github-actions-035-build-and-test-a-node-js-app","sec":"github-actions-s036","q":"Write a simple workflow to build and test a Node.js application.","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>name: Node.js CI\non: [push, pull_request]\njobs:\n  build:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v3\n        with: { node-version: &#x27;16&#x27;, cache: &#x27;npm&#x27; }\n      - run: npm ci\n      - run: npm run build\n      - run: npm test</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0069","card":"q-github-actions-035-build-and-test-a-node-js-app","sec":"github-actions-s036","q":"Run tests on push to main.","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on:\n  push:\n    branches:\n      - main\njobs:\n  test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - run: npm install &amp;&amp; npm test</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0070","card":"q-github-actions-035-build-and-test-a-node-js-app","sec":"github-actions-s036","q":"Run tests on a pull request to <code>develop</code> (Python).","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>name: Test PR\non:\n  pull_request:\n    branches: [develop]\njobs:\n  test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n      - uses: actions/setup-python@v4\n        with: { python-version: &#x27;3.9&#x27; }\n      - run: pip install -r requirements.txt\n      - run: pytest</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0071","card":"q-github-actions-035-build-and-test-a-node-js-app","sec":"github-actions-s036","q":"Build and test a Go app on push.","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on:\n  push:\n    branches: [&#x27;*&#x27;]\njobs:\n  build-test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n      - uses: actions/setup-go@v3\n        with: { go-version: &#x27;1.18&#x27; }\n      - run: go build ./...\n      - run: go test ./...</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0072","card":"q-github-actions-035-build-and-test-a-node-js-app","sec":"github-actions-s036","q":"Checkout the repo and list files.","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\njobs:\n  list:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n      - run: ls -la</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0073","card":"q-github-actions-036-linting","sec":"github-actions-s037","q":"Lint on push to main.","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>name: Lint Code\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\njobs:\n  lint:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v3\n        with: { node-version: &#x27;16&#x27; }\n      - run: npm install\n      - run: npm run lint</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0074","card":"q-github-actions-036-linting","sec":"github-actions-s037","q":"How do you run static analysis or linting in Python?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- run: pip install flake8\n- run: flake8 .</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0075","card":"q-github-actions-036-linting","sec":"github-actions-s037","q":"Lint a pull request and comment the result on it.","a":"<p>Save the report, flag a failure, then post it with <code>github-script</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on: pull_request\njobs:\n  lint:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - run: npm install\n      - id: lint\n        run: npm run lint -- --output-file eslint-report.txt || echo &quot;LINT_FAILED=true&quot; &gt;&gt; $GITHUB_ENV\n      - if: env.LINT_FAILED == &#x27;true&#x27;\n        uses: actions/github-script@v6\n        with:\n          script: |\n            const fs = require(&#x27;fs&#x27;);\n            const report = fs.readFileSync(&#x27;eslint-report.txt&#x27;, &#x27;utf8&#x27;);\n            github.rest.issues.createComment({\n              issue_number: context.issue.number,\n              owner: context.repo.owner,\n              repo: context.repo.repo,\n              body: `Linting failed:\\n\\`\\`\\`\\n${report}\\n\\`\\`\\``\n            });\n        env:\n          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0076","card":"q-github-actions-038-docker-images","sec":"github-actions-s039","q":"Build and push a Docker image.","a":"<p>Log in with <code>docker/login-action</code>, then use <code>docker/build-push-action</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on:\n  push:\n    branches:\n      - main\njobs:\n  build:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - uses: docker/login-action@v3\n        with:\n          username: ${{ secrets.DOCKER_USERNAME }}\n          password: ${{ secrets.DOCKER_PASSWORD }}\n      - uses: docker/build-push-action@v5\n        with:\n          push: true\n          tags: user/app:latest</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0077","card":"q-github-actions-038-docker-images","sec":"github-actions-s039","q":"Build and push to Docker Hub with plain docker commands.","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>name: Build Docker\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\njobs:\n  build:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n      - uses: docker/login-action@v2\n        with:\n          username: ${{ secrets.DOCKER_USERNAME }}\n          password: ${{ secrets.DOCKER_PASSWORD }}\n      - run: |\n          docker build -t ${{ secrets.DOCKER_USERNAME }}/my-app:latest .\n          docker push ${{ secrets.DOCKER_USERNAME }}/my-app:latest</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0078","card":"q-github-actions-039-deploying-to-aws","sec":"github-actions-s040","q":"How do you deploy to AWS (or another cloud)?","a":"<p>Use the provider's action, such as <code>aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials</code>, with credentials from secrets.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on:\n  push:\n    branches:\n      - main\njobs:\n  deploy:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - uses: aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials@v4\n        with:\n          aws-access-key-id: ${{ secrets.AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID }}\n          aws-secret-access-key: ${{ secrets.AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY }}\n          aws-region: us-east-1\n      - run: aws s3 sync ./dist/ s3://my-bucket/</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0079","card":"q-github-actions-040-deploy-after-tests-and-multi-stage-deplo","sec":"github-actions-s041","q":"How do you deploy only after tests pass?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>jobs:\n  test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - run: npm test\n  deploy:\n    needs: test\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - run: npm run deploy</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0080","card":"q-github-actions-040-deploy-after-tests-and-multi-stage-deplo","sec":"github-actions-s041","q":"How do you do a multi-stage deployment?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>jobs:\n  test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - run: npm test\n  deploy-dev:\n    needs: test\n    if: github.ref == &#x27;refs/heads/dev&#x27;\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - run: echo &quot;Deploy dev&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0081","card":"q-github-actions-041-releases-and-publishing","sec":"github-actions-s042","q":"Automate a GitHub release on a version tag.","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on:\n  push:\n    tags:\n      - &#x27;v*&#x27;\njobs:\n  release:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - uses: actions/create-release@v1\n        env:\n          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n        with:\n          tag_name: ${{ github.ref_name }}\n          release_name: Release ${{ github.ref_name }}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0082","card":"q-github-actions-041-releases-and-publishing","sec":"github-actions-s042","q":"Auto-bump a version and release.","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on: workflow_dispatch\njobs:\n  release:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - run: npm version patch &amp;&amp; git push --follow-tags\n      - uses: actions/create-release@v1\n        env:\n          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0083","card":"q-github-actions-041-releases-and-publishing","sec":"github-actions-s042","q":"How do you publish a package to npm or PyPI?","a":"<p>Authenticate with a secret and run the publish command.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- run: npm publish\n  env:\n    NODE_AUTH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.NPM_TOKEN }}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0084","card":"q-github-actions-041-releases-and-publishing","sec":"github-actions-s042","q":"Auto-release a Python package to PyPI on a tag push.","a":"<p>Trigger on tags, store the PyPI token as a secret, then build and publish with twine.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on:\n  push:\n    tags: [&#x27;v*&#x27;]\njobs:\n  publish:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - run: twine upload dist/*\n        env:\n          TWINE_PASSWORD: ${{ secrets.PYPI_TOKEN }}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0085","card":"q-github-actions-042-notifications","sec":"github-actions-s043","q":"Send Slack notifications.","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on: push\njobs:\n  notify:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - run: echo &quot;Running&quot;\n      - if: success() || failure()\n        uses: slackapi/slack-github-action@v1.26.0\n        with:\n          slack-bot-token: ${{ secrets.SLACK_BOT_TOKEN }}\n          channel-id: &#x27;my-channel&#x27;\n          text: &#x27;Workflow ${{ job.status }}!&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0086","card":"q-github-actions-042-notifications","sec":"github-actions-s043","q":"Send a Slack notification only on failure.","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>steps:\n  - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n  - run: exit 1\n  - if: failure()\n    uses: slackapi/slack-github-action@v1.23.0\n    with:\n      slack-bot-token: ${{ secrets.SLACK_BOT_TOKEN }}\n      channel-id: &#x27;general&#x27;\n      text: &#x27;Workflow failed!&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0087","card":"q-github-actions-043-auto-formatting-and-external-repos","sec":"github-actions-s044","q":"Automate code formatting and push the changes.","a":"<p>Run the formatter, commit with an action, and guard with <code>if</code> to avoid a loop.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- uses: stefanzweifel/git-auto-commit-action@v4\n  with:\n    commit_message: &quot;Auto-format&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0088","card":"q-github-actions-043-auto-formatting-and-external-repos","sec":"github-actions-s044","q":"Clone a repo from another organization and run a script.","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>steps:\n  - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n    with:\n      repository: other-org/other-repo\n      token: ${{ secrets.PAT }}\n  - run: ./script.sh</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0089","card":"q-github-actions-044-self-hosted-runner-and-debug-workflow","sec":"github-actions-s045","q":"How do you run a workflow on a self-hosted runner?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>runs-on: self-hosted</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0090","card":"q-github-actions-044-self-hosted-runner-and-debug-workflow","sec":"github-actions-s045","q":"How do you print debug output in a workflow?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>name: Debug Workflow\non: [push]\njobs:\n  debug:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - run: echo &quot;Debugging enabled&quot; &amp;&amp; ls -la\n        env:\n          ACTIONS_STEP_DEBUG: true</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0091","card":"q-github-actions-046-deploy-to-github-pages","sec":"github-actions-s047","q":"Deploy a static site to GitHub Pages on a tag.","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>name: Deploy Pages\non:\n  push:\n    tags: [&#x27;v*&#x27;]\njobs:\n  deploy:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n      - run: npm install &amp;&amp; npm run build\n      - uses: peaceiris/actions-gh-pages@v3\n        with:\n          github_token: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n          publish_dir: ./dist</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0092","card":"q-github-actions-051-monorepos","sec":"github-actions-s052","q":"Monorepo: run workflows for specific directory changes.","a":"<p>Use <code>paths</code> and conditional jobs.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on:\n  push:\n    paths: [&#x27;services/frontend/**&#x27;]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0093","card":"q-github-actions-053-debugging-a-failing-workflow","sec":"github-actions-s054","q":"How do you debug a failing GitHub Actions workflow?","a":"<p>Check the logs, add <code>echo</code> or debug steps, enable <code>ACTIONS_STEP_DEBUG</code>, re-run the workflow, or test locally with <code>act</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0094","card":"q-github-actions-058-limitations-of-github-actions","sec":"github-actions-s059","q":"What are the limitations (execution time, storage, concurrency)?","a":"<p>A 6-hour job limit, 500 MB artifact storage, limited concurrency on the free tier, and fixed runner specs.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0095","card":"q-github-actions-059-workflow-not-triggering-on-a-pr","sec":"github-actions-s060","q":"A workflow is not triggering on a PR. How do you troubleshoot?","a":"<p>Check the <code>on</code> block, permissions, branch and path filters, the logs and GitHub status.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on:\n  pull_request:\n    branches: [main]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0096","card":"q-github-actions-060-enforcing-tests-before-merge","sec":"github-actions-s061","q":"Enforce passing tests for PRs and prevent bypassing.","a":"<p>Enable branch protection, require status checks and limit merge permissions.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on: pull_request\njobs:\n  test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - run: npm test</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0097","card":"q-github-actions-060-enforcing-tests-before-merge","sec":"github-actions-s061","q":"A production deployment fails because of an outdated branch. How do you prevent it?","a":"<p>Restrict triggers to <code>main</code>, use tags and add approvals.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0098","card":"q-github-actions-061-service-containers","sec":"github-actions-s062","q":"The app needs a database for tests that the runners do not have. How do you set it up?","a":"<p>Use a service container such as PostgreSQL and configure the connection.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>services:\n  postgres:\n    image: postgres\n    env:\n      POSTGRES_DB: test</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0099","card":"q-github-actions-062-environment-problems","sec":"github-actions-s063","q":"A workflow fails because a tool version is missing. How do you handle it?","a":"<p>Install the tool, use a custom container or use a self-hosted runner.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>container: custom-image:1.0</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0100","card":"q-github-actions-062-environment-problems","sec":"github-actions-s063","q":"Test results are inconsistent across runners. How do you fix it?","a":"<p>Pin versions, use the same runner and control test randomness.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>container: node:16</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0101","card":"q-github-actions-062-environment-problems","sec":"github-actions-s063","q":"A legacy app needs a custom build environment. How do you address it?","a":"<p>Use a custom Docker image or a self-hosted runner.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>container: legacy-env:1.0</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0102","card":"q-github-actions-063-reporting-deployments","sec":"github-actions-s064","q":"Report successful deployments for the past month. How do you extract them?","a":"<p>Use the GitHub API, filter successes and automate the report.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- run: curl -H &quot;Authorization: Bearer ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}&quot; https://api.github.com/repos/${{ github.repository }}/deployments</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0103","card":"q-github-actions-064-migrating-from-jenkins","sec":"github-actions-s065","q":"What are the challenges of moving from Jenkins to GitHub Actions?","a":"<p>Learning YAML, setting up runners, migrating plugins and cost for private repos.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0104","card":"q-github-actions-065-how-python-fits-in","sec":"github-actions-s066","q":"How does Python integrate with GitHub Actions?","a":"<p>Python scripts can trigger workflows through the GitHub API or run as steps inside workflows to automate CI/CD tasks.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0105","card":"q-github-actions-065-how-python-fits-in","sec":"github-actions-s066","q":"How can GitHub Actions be orchestrated using Python scripts?","a":"<p>Run Python scripts as workflow steps for tests or deployment, use <code>PyGithub</code> to trigger workflows, manage repos or update issues, and use repository dispatch events to trigger workflows programmatically.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from github import Github\ng = Github(&quot;&lt;token&gt;&quot;)\nrepo = g.get_repo(&quot;owner/repo&quot;)\nrepo.create_repository_dispatch(event_type=&quot;trigger-workflow&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0106","card":"q-github-actions-065-how-python-fits-in","sec":"github-actions-s066","q":"How can Python automate or trigger workflows programmatically?","a":"<p>The same three approaches: run scripts in workflows, call the GitHub API with <code>PyGithub</code> (trigger workflows, manage PRs, update issues), and send repository dispatch events. The example above with <code>event_type=\"custom-event\"</code> works the same way.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0107","card":"q-github-actions-065-how-python-fits-in","sec":"github-actions-s066","q":"How do you ensure idempotency across these tools?","a":"<p>For GitHub Actions, use conditional steps to avoid redundant actions. For the other tools: Terraform uses state files, Ansible uses <code>state</code> parameters, boto3 checks existence before creating (for example <code>head_bucket</code>) and Kubernetes uses <code>apply</code> semantics.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0108","card":"q-github-actions-065-how-python-fits-in","sec":"github-actions-s066","q":"What are the best practices for structuring Python scripts that manage multiple tools, GitHub Actions included?","a":"<p>Modular design (a module per tool), config files, robust exception handling for API failures, the <code>logging</code> module, Git versioning and unit tests for critical functions.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0109","card":"q-github-actions-066-triggering-a-workflow-through-the-api","sec":"github-actions-s067","q":"How do you trigger a workflow programmatically via the GitHub API?","a":"<p>Use the \"Create a workflow dispatch event\" endpoint, <code>POST /repos/{owner}/{repo}/actions/workflows/{workflow_id}/dispatches</code>, with <code>requests</code> and a PAT. A 204 response means success.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import requests\ndef trigger_workflow(owner, repo, workflow_id, ref, token, inputs=None):\n    url = f&quot;https://api.github.com/repos/{owner}/{repo}/actions/workflows/{workflow_id}/dispatches&quot;\n    headers = {\n        &quot;Authorization&quot;: f&quot;Bearer {token}&quot;,\n        &quot;Accept&quot;: &quot;application/vnd.github.v3+json&quot;\n    }\n    data = {\n        &quot;ref&quot;: ref,  # Branch or tag to run the workflow on\n        &quot;inputs&quot;: inputs or {}\n    }\n    response = requests.post(url, json=data, headers=headers)\n    if response.status_code == 204:\n        print(&quot;Workflow triggered successfully!&quot;)\n    else:\n        print(f&quot;Failed to trigger workflow: {response.json()}&quot;)\n# Example usage\ntrigger_workflow(\n    owner=&quot;my-org&quot;,\n    repo=&quot;my-repo&quot;,\n    workflow_id=&quot;deploy.yml&quot;,\n    ref=&quot;main&quot;,\n    token=os.environ[&quot;GITHUB_TOKEN&quot;]\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0110","card":"q-github-actions-067-checking-run-status-and-listing-workflow","sec":"github-actions-s068","q":"How do you check the status of a workflow run with <code>PyGithub</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from github import Github\ndef check_workflow_status(owner, repo, run_id, token):\n    g = Github(token)\n    repo = g.get_repo(f&quot;{owner}/{repo}&quot;)\n    workflow_run = repo.get_workflow_run(run_id)\n    status = workflow_run.status\n    conclusion = workflow_run.conclusion\n    print(f&quot;Workflow Run ID: {run_id}&quot;)\n    print(f&quot;Status: {status}&quot;)\n    print(f&quot;Conclusion: {conclusion}&quot;)\n    return status, conclusion</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0111","card":"q-github-actions-067-checking-run-status-and-listing-workflow","sec":"github-actions-s068","q":"How do you list all workflows in a repository?","a":"<p>Use <code>GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/actions/workflows</code> or <code>PyGithub</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from github import Github\ndef list_workflows(owner, repo, token):\n    g = Github(token)\n    repo = g.get_repo(f&quot;{owner}/{repo}&quot;)\n    workflows = repo.get_workflows()\n    for workflow in workflows:\n        print(f&quot;Workflow: {workflow.name}, ID: {workflow.id}, Path: {workflow.path}&quot;)\n    return workflows</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0112","card":"q-github-actions-068-running-a-python-script-in-a-workflow","sec":"github-actions-s069","q":"How do you configure a workflow to run a Python script for resource management?","a":"<p>Set up Python, install dependencies, and run the script with secrets passed as environment variables.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>name: Run Python Script\non: [push]\njobs:\n  manage-resources:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n    - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n    - name: Set up Python\n      uses: actions/setup-python@v4\n      with:\n        python-version: &#x27;3.10&#x27;\n    - name: Install dependencies\n      run: pip install -r requirements.txt\n    - name: Run Python script\n      env:\n        AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID: ${{ secrets.AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID }}\n        AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY: ${{ secrets.AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY }}\n      run: python manage_resources.py</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0113","card":"q-github-actions-068-running-a-python-script-in-a-workflow","sec":"github-actions-s069","q":"How do you integrate GitHub Actions with AWS or Kubernetes using Python?","a":"<p>Use <code>boto3</code> for AWS (S3, EC2, EKS), the <code>kubernetes</code> client for clusters, pass credentials as secrets, and add retry logic and logging.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>name: Manage AWS and Kubernetes\non: [push]\njobs:\n  manage:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n    - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n    - name: Set up Python\n      uses: actions/setup-python@v4\n      with:\n        python-version: &#x27;3.10&#x27;\n    - name: Install dependencies\n      run: pip install boto3 kubernetes\n    - name: Run script\n      env:\n        AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID: ${{ secrets.AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID }}\n        AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY: ${{ secrets.AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY }}\n        KUBE_CONFIG: ${{ secrets.KUBE_CONFIG }}\n      run: python manage_resources.py</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0114","card":"q-github-actions-069-generating-workflow-files-with-python","sec":"github-actions-s070","q":"How do you create a workflow file dynamically with Python?","a":"<p>Write YAML into <code>.github/workflows</code>, using the <code>yaml</code> library for correct formatting.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import yaml\nimport os\ndef create_workflow_file(filename, workflow_name, trigger, steps):\n    workflow = {\n        &quot;name&quot;: workflow_name,\n        &quot;on&quot;: trigger,\n        &quot;jobs&quot;: {\n            &quot;build&quot;: {\n                &quot;runs-on&quot;: &quot;ubuntu-latest&quot;,\n                &quot;steps&quot;: steps\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    os.makedirs(&quot;.github/workflows&quot;, exist_ok=True)\n    with open(f&quot;.github/workflows/{filename}&quot;, &quot;w&quot;) as f:\n        yaml.dump(workflow, f, default_flow_style=False)\n    print(f&quot;Workflow file {filename} created!&quot;)\n# Example usage\nsteps = [\n    {&quot;uses&quot;: &quot;actions/checkout@v3&quot;},\n    {&quot;name&quot;: &quot;Set up Python&quot;, &quot;uses&quot;: &quot;actions/setup-python@v4&quot;, &quot;with&quot;: {&quot;python-version&quot;: &quot;3.10&quot;}},\n    {&quot;name&quot;: &quot;Run script&quot;, &quot;run&quot;: &quot;python script.py&quot;}\n]\ncreate_workflow_file(&quot;dynamic.yml&quot;, &quot;Dynamic Workflow&quot;, [&quot;push&quot;], steps)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0115","card":"q-github-actions-069-generating-workflow-files-with-python","sec":"github-actions-s070","q":"Scenario: automate creating workflows for multiple repositories.","a":"<p>Use <code>PyGithub</code> to create the workflow file in each repo, generating YAML from a template.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from github import Github\nimport yaml\ndef create_workflow_in_repo(owner, repo_name, token, workflow_name, steps):\n    g = Github(token)\n    repo = g.get_repo(f&quot;{owner}/{repo_name}&quot;)\n    workflow = {\n        &quot;name&quot;: workflow_name,\n        &quot;on&quot;: [&quot;push&quot;],\n        &quot;jobs&quot;: {\n            &quot;build&quot;: {\n                &quot;runs-on&quot;: &quot;ubuntu-latest&quot;,\n                &quot;steps&quot;: steps\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    workflow_content = yaml.dump(workflow, default_flow_style=False)\n    repo.create_file(\n        path=f&quot;.github/workflows/{workflow_name.lower()}.yml&quot;,\n        message=f&quot;Add {workflow_name} workflow&quot;,\n        content=workflow_content\n    )\n    print(f&quot;Workflow created in {repo_name}&quot;)\n# Example usage\nsteps = [\n    {&quot;uses&quot;: &quot;actions/checkout@v3&quot;},\n    {&quot;name&quot;: &quot;Run script&quot;, &quot;run&quot;: &quot;python script.py&quot;}\n]\ncreate_workflow_in_repo(&quot;my-org&quot;, &quot;my-repo&quot;, token, &quot;CI&quot;, steps)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0116","card":"q-github-actions-070-logs-and-secrets-through-the-api","sec":"github-actions-s071","q":"How do you download workflow logs with the GitHub API?","a":"<p>Use <code>GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/actions/runs/{run_id}/logs</code>, which returns a ZIP file.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import requests\nimport zipfile\nimport io\ndef download_workflow_logs(owner, repo, run_id, token):\n    url = f&quot;https://api.github.com/repos/{owner}/{repo}/actions/runs/{run_id}/logs&quot;\n    headers = {\n        &quot;Authorization&quot;: f&quot;Bearer {token}&quot;,\n        &quot;Accept&quot;: &quot;application/vnd.github.v3+json&quot;\n    }\n    response = requests.get(url, headers=headers, stream=True)\n    if response.status_code == 200:\n        with zipfile.ZipFile(io.BytesIO(response.content)) as z:\n            z.extractall(&quot;workflow_logs&quot;)\n        print(&quot;Logs downloaded and extracted!&quot;)\n    else:\n        print(f&quot;Failed to download logs: {response.status_code}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0117","card":"q-github-actions-070-logs-and-secrets-through-the-api","sec":"github-actions-s071","q":"How can Python automate the creation of Actions secrets?","a":"<p>Use <code>PUT /repos/{owner}/{repo}/actions/secrets/{secret_name}</code>. The value must be encrypted with the repository's public key (PyNaCl sealed box).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from github import Github\nfrom nacl import public\ndef create_secret(owner, repo, secret_name, secret_value, token):\n    g = Github(token)\n    repo = g.get_repo(f&quot;{owner}/{repo}&quot;)\n    public_key = repo.get_public_key()\n    public_key_obj = public.PublicKey(public_key.key.encode(), encoder=public.Base64Encoder)\n    sealed_box = public.SealedBox(public_key_obj)\n    encrypted_value = sealed_box.encrypt(secret_value.encode())\n    repo.create_secret(secret_name, encrypted_value.hex())\n    print(f&quot;Secret {secret_name} created!&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0118","card":"q-github-actions-071-api-tokens-and-rate-limits","sec":"github-actions-s072","q":"How do you secure GitHub API tokens in Python scripts for Actions automation?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Store tokens in Actions secrets and read them with <code>${{ secrets.TOKEN }}</code>.</li>\n  <li>Pass secrets to scripts as environment variables.</li>\n  <li>Never hardcode tokens in scripts or the repo.</li>\n  <li>Use short-lived tokens with minimal permissions.</li>\n  <li>Audit and rotate tokens regularly.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>name: Secure Python Script\non: [push]\njobs:\n  run-script:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n    - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n    - name: Run Python script\n      env:\n        GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n      run: python script.py</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0119","card":"q-github-actions-071-api-tokens-and-rate-limits","sec":"github-actions-s072","q":"How do you handle GitHub API rate limits in Python?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Monitor the <code>X-RateLimit-Remaining</code> header.</li>\n  <li>Use exponential backoff (<code>backoff</code>, <code>ratelimit</code>).</li>\n  <li>On HTTP 429, wait for the <code>Retry-After</code> duration.</li>\n  <li>Use conditional requests (ETags, <code>If-Modified-Since</code>) to reduce calls.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import requests\nimport time\ndef make_github_request(url, token):\n    headers = {&quot;Authorization&quot;: f&quot;Bearer {token}&quot;, &quot;Accept&quot;: &quot;application/vnd.github.v3+json&quot;}\n    response = requests.get(url, headers=headers)\n    if response.status_code == 429:\n        retry_after = int(response.headers.get(&quot;Retry-After&quot;, 60))\n        time.sleep(retry_after)\n        return make_github_request(url, token)\n    response.raise_for_status()\n    return response.json()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0120","card":"q-github-actions-072-python-scenarios","sec":"github-actions-s073","q":"Scenario: a workflow is not triggering for a specific branch. How would Python troubleshoot via the GitHub API?","a":"<p>Use <code>PyGithub</code> to read the workflow file, check its <code>on</code> branch filter, and inspect branch protection rules.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from github import Github\ndef troubleshoot_workflow(owner, repo, workflow_path, branch, token):\n    g = Github(token)\n    repo = g.get_repo(f&quot;{owner}/{repo}&quot;)\n    # Check workflow file\n    try:\n        workflow_content = repo.get_contents(workflow_path).decoded_content.decode()\n        print(&quot;Workflow content:&quot;, workflow_content)\n        if f&quot;branches: [{branch}]&quot; not in workflow_content:\n            print(f&quot;Branch {branch} not configured in workflow&quot;)\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f&quot;Error reading workflow file: {e}&quot;)\n    # Check branch protection\n    branch_obj = repo.get_branch(branch)\n    if branch_obj.protected:\n        print(&quot;Branch is protected. Check protection rules.&quot;)\n        print(branch_obj.get_protection())</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0121","card":"q-github-actions-073-python-scenarios-debugging-and-credentia","sec":"github-actions-s074","q":"Scenario: a workflow fails because of a dependency issue in a Python script. How do you debug it?","a":"<p>Check the logs, reproduce locally with the same environment, pin versions in <code>requirements.txt</code>, add debug output, and install dependencies in a separate step to isolate issues.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>name: Debug Python Script\non: [push]\njobs:\n  debug:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n    - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n    - name: Set up Python\n      uses: actions/setup-python@v4\n      with:\n        python-version: &#x27;3.10&#x27;\n    - name: Install dependencies\n      run: pip install -r requirements.txt\n    - name: Run script with debug\n      run: python -m trace --trace script.py</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0122","card":"q-github-actions-073-python-scenarios-debugging-and-credentia","sec":"github-actions-s074","q":"Scenario: a workflow exposes AWS credentials in logs. How do you secure it?","a":"<p>Store credentials in secrets, make sure sensitive data is not printed, and check Python scripts for accidental logging.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>name: Secure AWS Workflow\non: [push]\njobs:\n  deploy:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n    - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n    - name: Set up Python\n      uses: actions/setup-python@v4\n      with:\n        python-version: &#x27;3.10&#x27;\n    - name: Run script\n      env:\n        AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID: ${{ secrets.AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID }}\n        AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY: ${{ secrets.AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY }}\n      run: python deploy.py</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code># deploy.py\nimport boto3\nimport os\ndef deploy():\n    # Avoid printing credentials\n    session = boto3.Session(\n        aws_access_key_id=os.getenv(&quot;AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID&quot;),\n        aws_secret_access_key=os.getenv(&quot;AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY&quot;)\n    )\n    s3 = session.client(&quot;s3&quot;)\n    s3.list_buckets()  # Example operation\n    print(&quot;Deployment completed&quot;)\ndeploy()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0123","card":"q-github-actions-074-role-of-github-actions-in-test-automatio","sec":"github-actions-s075","q":"How do Python, Bash and GitHub Actions complement each other?","a":"<p>Python writes robust test scripts, Bash handles environment setup and CLI tasks, and GitHub Actions orchestrates the workflows and triggers the tests.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0124","card":"q-github-actions-074-role-of-github-actions-in-test-automatio","sec":"github-actions-s075","q":"What is the role of GitHub Actions in automating testing?","a":"<p>It triggers tests on events, runs them in isolated runners, integrates tools and provides reports.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0125","card":"q-github-actions-074-role-of-github-actions-in-test-automatio","sec":"github-actions-s075","q":"What are the benefits of running tests in CI/CD with GitHub Actions?","a":"<p>Quality assurance, fast feedback, parallel execution, deployment automation and report generation.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0126","card":"q-github-actions-074-role-of-github-actions-in-test-automatio","sec":"github-actions-s075","q":"How do you secure sensitive data in test automation?","a":"<p>Use GitHub Secrets, avoid hardcoding, restrict access and encrypt local files.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0127","card":"q-github-actions-074-role-of-github-actions-in-test-automatio","sec":"github-actions-s075","q":"What are the limitations of GitHub Actions for test automation?","a":"<p>Limited free minutes, a 6-hour job limit, artifact storage caps, dependence on GitHub and less orchestration flexibility.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0128","card":"q-github-actions-075-running-tests","sec":"github-actions-s076","q":"How do you run Python tests with pytest in GitHub Actions?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>name: Tests\non: [push]\njobs:\n  test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n    - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n    - uses: actions/setup-python@v4\n      with: { python-version: &#x27;3.10&#x27; }\n    - run: pip install pytest\n    - run: pytest</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0129","card":"q-github-actions-075-running-tests","sec":"github-actions-s076","q":"How do you run matrix builds for multiple Python versions?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>strategy:\n  matrix:\n    python-version: [&#x27;3.8&#x27;, &#x27;3.9&#x27;, &#x27;3.10&#x27;]\nsteps:\n- uses: actions/setup-python@v4\n  with: { python-version: ${{ matrix.python-version }} }</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0130","card":"q-github-actions-075-running-tests","sec":"github-actions-s076","q":"How do you run Python and Bash tests together?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>steps:\n- uses: actions/checkout@v3\n- uses: actions/setup-python@v4\n  with: { python-version: &#x27;3.10&#x27; }\n- run: pip install pytest\n- run: pytest\n- run: bash scripts/test.sh</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0131","card":"q-github-actions-075-running-tests","sec":"github-actions-s076","q":"How do you integrate a Bash script into a workflow?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>steps:\n- uses: actions/checkout@v3\n- run: bash scripts/test.sh</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0132","card":"q-github-actions-075-running-tests","sec":"github-actions-s076","q":"How do you integrate flake8 in a workflow?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>steps:\n- uses: actions/setup-python@v4\n  with: { python-version: &#x27;3.10&#x27; }\n- run: pip install flake8\n- run: flake8 .</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0133","card":"q-github-actions-076-triggers-reports-and-failures","sec":"github-actions-s077","q":"How do you trigger tests manually or on a schedule?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on:\n  workflow_dispatch:\n  schedule:\n    - cron: &#x27;0 0 * * *&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0134","card":"q-github-actions-076-triggers-reports-and-failures","sec":"github-actions-s077","q":"How do you schedule Bash tests?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on:\n  schedule:\n    - cron: &#x27;0 0 * * *&#x27;\nsteps:\n- uses: actions/checkout@v3\n- run: bash scripts/test.sh</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0135","card":"q-github-actions-076-triggers-reports-and-failures","sec":"github-actions-s077","q":"How do you upload test reports as artifacts?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- uses: actions/upload-artifact@v3\n  with:\n    name: coverage-report\n    path: coverage.xml</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0136","card":"q-github-actions-076-triggers-reports-and-failures","sec":"github-actions-s077","q":"How do you handle test failures?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- run: pytest\n  continue-on-error: true\n- run: echo &quot;Log failure&quot;\n  if: failure()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0137","card":"q-github-actions-076-triggers-reports-and-failures","sec":"github-actions-s077","q":"How do you debug failing tests?","a":"<p>Enable <code>ACTIONS_STEP_DEBUG</code>, add verbose output and upload logs.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- run: pytest -v\n- uses: actions/upload-artifact@v3\n  if: failure()\n  with: { name: logs, path: test_output.log }</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0138","card":"q-github-actions-076-triggers-reports-and-failures","sec":"github-actions-s077","q":"How do you secure environment variables?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>env:\n  API_KEY: ${{ secrets.API_KEY }}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0139","card":"q-github-actions-077-test-automation-scenarios-environment-an","sec":"github-actions-s078","q":"The workflow is too slow. How do you optimize it?","a":"<p>Cache dependencies, parallelize, run affected tests and use faster runners.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- uses: actions/cache@v3\n  with:\n    path: ~/.cache/pip\n    key: pip-${{ hashFiles(&#x27;requirements.txt&#x27;) }}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0140","card":"q-github-actions-077-test-automation-scenarios-environment-an","sec":"github-actions-s078","q":"A Bash script fails because of a missing dependency. How do you resolve it?","a":"<p>Install the dependency, use Docker or check for tools.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- run: sudo apt-get install -y jq\n- run: bash scripts/test.sh</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0141","card":"q-github-actions-077-test-automation-scenarios-environment-an","sec":"github-actions-s078","q":"How do you ensure PRs pass tests before merging?","a":"<p>Enable branch protection and require the test workflow status.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on: [pull_request]\nsteps:\n- run: pytest</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0142","card":"q-github-actions-077-test-automation-scenarios-environment-an","sec":"github-actions-s078","q":"A test script exposes credentials in logs. How do you mitigate it?","a":"<p>Use secrets, mask logs and audit scripts.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>env:\n  DB_PASS: ${{ secrets.DB_PASS }}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0143","card":"q-github-actions-077-test-automation-scenarios-environment-an","sec":"github-actions-s078","q":"How do you set up a test database?","a":"<p>Use a service container such as PostgreSQL.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>services:\n  postgres:\n    image: postgres\n    env:\n      POSTGRES_DB: test\n    ports: [&#x27;5432:5432&#x27;]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0144","card":"q-github-actions-077-test-automation-scenarios-environment-an","sec":"github-actions-s078","q":"How do you automate a daily test report?","a":"<p>Schedule the workflow, run a Python report script and upload the artifact.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on:\n  schedule:\n    - cron: &#x27;0 0 * * *&#x27;\nsteps:\n- run: python generate_report.py\n- uses: actions/upload-artifact@v3\n  with:\n    name: report\n    path: report.txt</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0145","card":"q-github-actions-078-test-automation-scenarios-platforms-and","sec":"github-actions-s079","q":"A Bash script fails on Windows runners. How do you fix it?","a":"<p>Use portable commands, check the OS or use Unix runners.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>[ &quot;$OSTYPE&quot; = &quot;msys&quot; ] &amp;&amp; dir || ls</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0146","card":"q-github-actions-078-test-automation-scenarios-platforms-and","sec":"github-actions-s079","q":"Monorepo: run tests only for specific directories.","a":"<p>Use <code>paths</code> filters.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on:\n  push:\n    paths: [&#x27;frontend/**&#x27;]\njobs:\n  frontend:\n    steps:\n    - run: npm test --prefix frontend</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0147","card":"q-github-actions-078-test-automation-scenarios-platforms-and","sec":"github-actions-s079","q":"A workflow does not trigger on PRs. How do you troubleshoot?","a":"<p>Check <code>on: pull_request</code>, branch rules, file paths and permissions.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>on: [pull_request]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0148","card":"q-github-actions-078-test-automation-scenarios-platforms-and","sec":"github-actions-s079","q":"How do you get a custom test environment?","a":"<p>Use a Docker container or a self-hosted runner.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>container: custom-image:latest</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"github-actions-f0149","card":"q-github-actions-078-test-automation-scenarios-platforms-and","sec":"github-actions-s079","q":"A test fails because of a dependency version mismatch. How do you ensure consistency?","a":"<p>Pin versions in <code>requirements.txt</code>, cache, and use a fixed Python version.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- uses: actions/setup-python@v4\n  with: { python-version: &#x27;3.10&#x27; }\n- run: pip install -r requirements.txt</code></pre></div>","hand":false}];
